# 131 · UX fixes found in use: the screens' small faults that the owner reports

**Status:** `PROPOSED` · **Version:** [v0.1.4](../roadmap.md#v014)

## What

A list of small faults in the dashboard's screens, found while the owner uses Thermite. Each item says what is wrong, what to do, and the pages that describe the screen. New reports are added here as they come. A fault that needs more than a small change gets a goal of its own.

### 1. A campaign's Agents' context lists rigs that have nothing to do with the campaign

- **What is wrong.** On a campaign's page, the block **Agents' context** has the table **What applies on each rig**, with one row for each rig that *can* run the campaign: each rig with the campaign's hardware. A campaign that runs on a CPU can run on every rig, so the table lists every rig, including rigs where no run of the campaign has ever been. The owner, 2026-10-24: "this shows up on a campaigns page even though its listing rigs that have nothing to do with this campaign".
- **What to do.** The table shows the rigs that matter to this campaign: the rigs its runs are at work on, then the rigs its earlier runs used. The other rigs that could run it are folded under one line, such as "3 other rigs can run it", which opens to show them. A campaign with no run yet says where a run can start, in one line, with the rigs folded the same way.
- **Pages:** [Start a campaign from the dashboard](../../_site/src/content/docs/how-to/campaigns/start-from-dashboard.md#set-the-agents-context) (step 3 of "Set the agents' context"), and the ⓘ of **What applies on each rig** (`src/control/ui/campaigns/context/index.ts`).

### 2. Export shows its status and progress once it is clicked

- **What is wrong.** **Export** on a rig's or a run's page sends the rig an export command, and the button says that the command was sent. A full export takes minutes: the rig writes it, then sends it to control, and only then does it show on the **Exports** page. Until then, nothing on the page says where it is. The owner, 2026-10-24: "a feature enhancement to show export status/progress once clicked".
- **What to do.** Once clicked, the page follows the export to its end, as a rig check's button does (goal 080): sent, written by the rig with its size, sent to control, then a link to download it on the **Exports** page, or the error in words. MCP's and REST's answers for the export give the same states.
- **Pages:** [Get a rig's results from control](../../_site/src/content/docs/how-to/operate/exports-on-control.md), and the export reference (`reference/exports.md`).

### 3. A run's page doesn't say when its lanes take turns

- **What is wrong.** A campaign's **Agents working at once** (the contract's `lanes.count`) is how many lanes the planner plans. The rig's **Workers at a time** on **Edit rig** is how many trials run at the same moment, one by default. When a run has more lanes than the rig has workers, the lanes take turns, and nothing on the run's page or the campaign's page says so. The owner, 2026-10-24, on a research run on a rig with one worker at a time: "it seems that it doesn't work its multiple lanes in parallel?"
- **What to do.** Where a run's lanes show (its Overview and Live, and the campaign's **Where it runs**), a line says when the rig's **Workers at a time** is below the run's lanes, such as "3 lanes, 1 worker at a time on this rig: the lanes take turns", with a link to **Edit rig**. `get_run` gives both numbers. Starting a run on a rig with fewer workers than lanes says the same before it starts.
- **Pages:** [Agents, lanes and the planner](../../_site/src/content/docs/explanation/agents-lanes-planner.md) (how many lanes run at once), [Start a campaign from the dashboard](../../_site/src/content/docs/how-to/campaigns/start-from-dashboard.md#5-where-it-runs), and the run's page.

### 4. Archive a campaign from the left navigation

- **What is wrong.** To archive a campaign, the owner opens its page, presses **⋯** and then **Archive**. Clearing out finished campaigns takes a page load each. The owner, 2026-10-24: "right click campaigns on sidebar to archive".
- **What to do.** A right-click on a campaign in the left navigation opens a small menu with **Archive**. The keyboard's menu key (or Shift+F10) on a focused campaign opens it too. Archive does what **Archive** under **⋯** does, with the same refusal in words while a run is at work or waits to start (`Not archived. Pause or close its runs first. …`). The line under the list says `Archived sort-speed.`, with **Undo**, which unarchives it. The browser's own menu stays everywhere else.
- **Pages:** [Archive campaigns and sort them into folders](../../_site/src/content/docs/how-to/campaigns/archive-and-folders.md#archive-a-campaign).

## Why

The owner reports these from use, 2026-10-24: "ux fixes to add".

## Constraints

- **A mockup first** ([rules for every goal](../README.md#rules-for-every-goal)): a real change to a screen is mocked up and shown to the owner before it is built.
- **Docs follow the code:** each fix updates the pages that describe its screen, and their screenshots, in the same commit.

## Done when

- [ ] Each item is fixed, after the owner approved its mockup, with its pages updated, or it moved to a goal of its own.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-24, owner: the UX fixes found in use go in v0.1.4, the UI clean-up and UX improvements.

## Open questions

- Item 1: whether the rigs where the campaign's runs ended long ago count as rigs that matter, or only the rigs of its runs at work and its latest run.
- Item 4: whether the menu also holds **Move to folder** and **Open**, or **Archive** alone.

## Progress

- 2026-10-24: Goal written, with item 1 from the owner's report.
- 2026-10-24: Item 2, export status and progress, from the owner's report.
- 2026-10-24: Item 3, a run's lanes that take turns on a rig with fewer workers at a time, from the owner's report. The rig had 1 worker at a time; raised to 3 over `set_rig_settings`.
- 2026-10-24: Item 4, archive a campaign from the left navigation's right-click menu, from the owner's report.

